 with the 12th doctor you and i  need to go have a conversation somewhere  so i can pick your brain and figure out  where you are getting any of that but  since he's putting it in the context of  a romantic talk i just  i just heavily disagree with that very  statement but i just need to say that so  we can get it done and focus on the  first part and when i said things don't  quite line up with what mandip said i  don't have an exact quote from her  because i didn't think to write it down  at the time but what she said when riley  silverman asked her  when did you know  that it was going to happen  mandip gil said when i read it on the  page meaning in eve of the daleks when  she read that dan asks yaz about this  and yaz confesses that was the first  time she knew it was happening i've  never told anyone now on the surface  this would seem to be a little bit of a  contradiction right because we have on  the one hand matt strevin saying jody  brought it to us after the first season  and so it was in our minds  very you know from that point on which  would have meant all through series 12  and all through flux yet it wasn't  addressed until after that but mandep  gill is saying no i did not know  until eve of the daleks  so what's going on here  well  a couple of things the first is is that  i would not be surprised if in both  cases there is a mild bit of  exaggeration going on i don't think  either one is a liar but i do think that  when you're especially at something like  a panel you tweak stories so that they  are better stories  they tell better and they hit better  that's just kind of a thing that happens  whether you mean it to or not  so i would not be surprised if the  impression that matt strevins left of  them sort of jumping on the idea once  jody whittaker brought it to them and  it's also worth saying that he said  amanda uh gill was in favor of the idea  and for him to imply that like they were  working on it ever since then  maybe that was the point at which the  seed was planted  but  that doesn't necessarily mean that they  were definitely writing them that way  from there on out  but to imply that kind of makes a better  story as for mandip gill i would not be  very surprised to learn that she had an  inclination a thought a hope that maybe  they would do it prior to that reveal  but  that she didn't know for certain until  she read it but she  but she didn't imply that she had  thought it would happen too much prior  to that so between those i think that  covers the gap in understanding and so  now  let's talk about how this came about and  also it's worth pointing out some people  are like reporting this in weird ways  like i saw some headlines that said  mandip gil and jody whitaker like fought  to have it happen i'm like nothing  either of them said implied that it was  like they were pushing and were arguing  and saying like we need this to happen  like that that wording i've seen in a  few places like no that's just a  complete  mischaracterization  of what i have heard and said and read  so drop that idea  but  what appears to have happened is that  series 11 it was on nobody's minds and  then after that series aired the fan  community some of them started talking  about this idea which  all fan communities have shippers they  just do so it's not exactly a novel  thing that that happened but the fact  that it got um to the creators and that  it was specifically brought to them by  one of their stars by jody whitaker and  was sort of co-signed as an idea by  mandip gill  that's sort of what makes it a little  bit more unusual because like as i said  every fandom has its shippers this stuff  happens for every show every season all  the time forever  so  the fact that the ship exists really  isn't the thing the thing is that it got  brought to the creative team  by some of their leads which would have  given it in theory more weight for them  to actually think about doing it  we know thasman was not planned since  series 11.  everybody's story indicates that that  was not going on  so that brings us to the question of  whether or not it was planned from the  start of series 12 on  and if it was  why didn't you tell your actors  that you were doing this  because the thing that really jumped out  to me about mandep's statement was that  it meant one of two things  on its own and then matt stress kind of  narrowed it down but at the time i heard  that i thought well that means one of  two things  either  chibnall decided to do that  kind of out of nowhere and like hadn't  really thought about it before but then  just decided to do it for whatever  reason  or  it meant he'd been planning it but for  some reason thought it was a good idea  to not tell the actors who had to  portray that  and it appears to be that second one  based off what matt strevin said with  them  kind of glomming onto the idea from jody  whitaker now that doesn't mean that  right from the start of series 12 that  they that the writers when i say they in  this case i mean the writers not also  the actors that they were planning to  implement it definitely from there on  out  but  man dipkill did know that she was going  to stick around for another series after  ryan and graham left  so  that definitely feels like it might have  been building towards this thing but  then why wouldn't you tell your actors  that's the thing that strikes me as  really  really strange the only argument that i  can think of that makes  any degree of sense  is that  maybe they were afraid that she might um  spill the beans like at a con or asked  by a fan or something which i'm not  gonna say is a totally invalid fear if  that was at play mendip gill herself um  at the panel was sort of adorably antsy  about like oh what can i say what can i  say  but the thing is like she had an  awareness  she was thinking very carefully about  that and wasn't like just dropping  things and going and then going oh no i  shouldn't have 