y ever went that direction it  could work that way  not the same thing as deliberately  playing it as love  but playing it in a way that  if they ever pulled the trigger on it  being love  the performance works for that  so we're in this bizarre situation where  the actress  and the fandom  kind of  manifested it to the writers  who then  after sitting on it for a bit did decide  to actually pull the trigger  now we've only got a couple of episodes  left to find out where if anywhere this  goes there's been assurance that it is  going to come up and be addressed in the  upcoming legend of the sea devils and i  really hope so because as we near the  end of the chibnall era  it's been frustrating how many of the  ideas the big ideas like them or not  have not actually yielded much  story  the  redestruction of gallifrey  has not really yielded any direct  stories  the timeless child  has  barely come up again and when it has  it's kind of been punted as if well  we'll deal with that later like you have  almost no time left  but you're not actively engaging with  these ideas and i would hate  the idea as much as i'm not a shipper  and i don't love the idea of the doctor  being in romantic relationships with the  companions or even them being one-sided  as much as i don't like that idea  if you're gonna have it  explore it  do something with it you're running out  of time  and that i feel  is  indicative of chibnall's era as a  showrunner more than anything else  that these ideas  while i can't say definitively they  aren't planned  the planning doesn't seem to actually  extend out very far  like the plan of what to do  after this thing that you built up to  like the timeless child happens okay so  what now  uh or you know the lack of planning in  the sense of  this whole thasman thing and the fact  that  the actress  didn't  know  so  again either you  made a late decision to make it canon  even though you knew about it much  sooner  or you just didn't tell her  what s